        "stdout": "Courier Relay protocol selection: an omitted \"protocol\" key selects the current protocol version (constant CURRENT_PROTOCOL in main.py, \"2\" as of 2026-09-07 after trial-1mb; it was \"1\" before that). An explicit supported version selects that version; protocol \"1\" remains supported explicitly and keeps its original contract ((account_id, delivery_id) identity, earliest occurred_at UTC instant wins, ties on smallest record_id). Protocol \"2\" — adopted permanently by the provider and approved by the integration owner as current in trial-1mb — identifies a delivery by delivery_id alone across all accounts, accepts the receipt with the latest occurred_at UTC instant (ties on smallest record_id), and presents accepted receipts in input order with original fields and timestamp spelling. A known command with an explicit unsupported/unknown protocol version returns {\"error\":\"unknown_protocol\"}; unknown commands still return {\"error\":\"unknown_command\"} regardless of protocol. Protocol handlers are dispatched via PROTOCOLS in main.py: command -> version -> handler. Decided while implementing trial-gbn (count, protocol 1) and revised in trial-1mb (protocol 2 current); future protocol-version issues should keep both error shapes stable.\n",
